# `*T` is exclusive at compile time, and the caller's loan on a `*T` it
# crossed (`ownership.md`, "Pointer Loans") lasts the call, which a
# function-value call never elides, so an alias's write panics
# `borrow-conflict`. Through a `*mut` with no reference
# (closure-field-call-through-a-counted-reference) the count stays.
